  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe downward bias during high-volatility correction phases; when recent history shows a sharp drop (e.g., from ~90 to ~58) followed by recovery, the model underestimates the rebound magnitude by 10-15%.",
    "Sentiment spikes (values > 0.33) preceding a forecast horizon correlate with significantly higher true outcomes than predicted; apply a positive correction factor of +4 to +6 EUR/ton when sentiment rises above 0.33 in the last 3 days.",
    "The model fails to capture mean reversion after extreme lows; if the last 5 days show prices below 70 EUR/ton, the forecast should be adjusted upward by at least 12% to reflect historical volatility recovery patterns.",
    "Forecast errors are largest in the first 10-14 days of the horizon; the model assumes a linear decline or stagnation while true outcomes show an immediate V-shaped bounce within the first week.",
    "When sentiment history shows a trailing increase (e.g., 0.33 -> 0.50 -> 1.00) alongside rising recent prices, the model's flatlining forecast is systematically too low by approximately 8-12 EUR/ton."
  ]
}
